Join the banking revolution! As the global leader in Engagement Banking, Backbase is at the forefront of revolutionizing banking services through technology. Our team is committed to developing cutting-edge tools and applications that empower our R&D organization and drive innovation. We are looking for a skilled System Engineer with a strong focus on Azure to join our global L3 team.


The L3 team is responsible for managing customers as well as internal runtimes - banks - and in that regard, we hold ourselves accountable to the highest professional standards in cloud ops. Resilience, Availability, and Scalability.



* Implement, and manage Azure cloud infrastructure to ensure our customers have access to the best features Azure has to offer.
* Implement and contribute to best practices for cloud security, compliance, and disaster recovery.
* Ensure that the solution always runs in a compliant, secure and cost-effective way.
* Ensure maximum reliability, high availability and uptime of the managed hosting service we provide to our customers..
* Help foster a culture of continuous learning and improvement.
* Troubleshoot and resolve infrastructure-related issues, ensuring resilience, availability and scalability.
* Contribute to increasing operational efficiency and helping to bring overall cloud cost under control.
* You have a deep understanding of cloud infrastructure security, cloud-native technologies, and desired state configuration,
* You are proficient with tools and tech like GitHub, Kubernetes, ArgoCD, Istio.
* You feel comfortable with the Grafana observability solution.
* You have strong communication skills allowing you to drive initiatives and decisions inside and outside your team;
* You have at least 3 years of experience in system engineering including at least 2 years of working with Azure cloud services;
* Your Azure competencies include but are not limited to Azure Front Door, WAF, Azure Service Bus, Azure SQL Database, Azure Regions, Availability Zones and DR.
* You combine technical excellence with mentorship skills, and provide your peers with hands-on guidance and collaborative problem-solving.
* You are focused on automation-first. Not content with anything manual, your goal is to make every process predictable and automated;
* You have a proven track record of implementing scalable, highly-available cloud infrastructure;
* Evidence of significant work experience with Azure is a plus;
* Work experience as software developer is a plus;
* Networking experience, including VPN configuration, is a plus;
* DB administration experience, including Azure SQL configuration, is a plus;
* Your English communication skills are excellent.

**Our Company**
 Oaktree is a leader among global investment managers specializing in alternative investments, with more than $220 billion in assets under management. The firm emphasizes an opportunistic, value\-oriented, and risk\-controlled approach to investments in credit, equity, and real estate. The firm has more than 1,400 employees and offices in more than 25 cities worldwide.




 We are committed to cultivating an environment that is collaborative, curious, inclusive and honors diversity of thought. Providing training and career development opportunities and emphasizing strong support for our local communities through philanthropic initiatives are essential to our culture.




 For additional information, please visit Oaktree’s website at http://www.oaktreecapital.com/




**Role Description**
* Providing quality and timely administrative support to the Luxembourg Cosec team;
* Electronic filing, creation and maintenance of e\-files;
* Saving and sorting transactional documentation;
* Collecting signatures on NDAs, other standard documents and quarterly board meetings;
* Creating and updating structure charts, liaising with the relevant parties;
* Maintenance of various Lux internal databases;
* Organizing internal and external meetings or appointments; and
* Assisting with ad hoc secretarial / administrative tasks and other projects as necessary.


**Required Experience**
* At least 1\-2 years in a corporate secretarial or administration function;
* Experience of managing a large number of requests and demonstrating an exceptional focus on prioritizing tasks and meeting deadlines;
* Strong organizational skills and good knowledge of the Microsoft Office pack; and
* Basic Luxembourg Corporate Law and Governance knowledge is an asset.


**Education**
 Bachelor’s degree required.




